{
  "task_id": "public-settings-001",
  "success": true,
  "final_answer": "All checks pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was in `settings.py`: `parse_settings` used `dict(line.split(\"=\") for line in text.splitlines())`, which:\n- crashed on blank/whitespace-only lines (no `=` to unpack),\n- crashed when a value contained `=` (too many values to unpack),\n- didn't trim spaces around names/values.\n\n**Fix** — rewrote `parse_settings` to:\n1. Skip lines that are empty or whitespace-only (`if not line.strip(): continue`).\n2. Split at the **first** `=` using `line.partition(\"=\")`, so `=` inside values is preserved.\n3. Trim whitespace from both the name and the value with `.strip()`.\n4. Return an empty dict for empty input (the loop simply never runs).\n\nVerified with `python -B public_checks.py` (the blank-line reproduction now passes) plus extra edge cases: empty input, whitespace-only input, padded names/values, values containing `=`, and empty values — all pass. Only `settings.py` was edited; no new files were created.",
